Setup custom authentication for litellm.
* Add an option to define users in the litellm configuration ("lite-llm/config.nix"). The key *is not* part of these options. 
* The launch wrapper, defined in "lite-llm/setup.nix", will check the list of defined users and generate random keys before starting
  litellm. Keys should be re-used if there were generated previously.
* A custom litellm authenticator will be defined based on the users and credentials. The authenticator
  will check if the request matches a known user and key.
* The litellm runtime runtime configuration, generated in "lite-llm/setup.nix", must enable the authenticator.
  Note that that requires that the authenticator reside in the same directory as the yaml configuration.

